WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.767
A good way to understand recursion is to trace a few iterations by hand.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:08.482
Start with the anchor. That is iteration zero.

00:00:08.482 --> 00:00:12.607
Next, use those rows to find the first set of children.

00:00:12.607 --> 00:00:15.652
Then use those children to find the next level.

00:00:15.652 --> 00:00:19.647
Continue until the recursive step returns no new rows.

00:00:19.647 --> 00:00:26.867
If a recursive query is confusing, use a tiny dataset and write down what appears at each iteration.

00:00:26.867 --> 00:00:31.102
That is often much easier than staring at the full S Q L statement.
